<h2>Which filter layout fits the activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Real sample rows. Wireframe fidelity only: final colors, sizes, and spacing come from the guideline tokens.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Three views + week select</h3>
      <p>A "Show" radio group (All events / Failed sign-ins / Security changes) and one "Week" select listing the ~13 weeks in the 90-day window. Two controls, one click each. Matches the stated jobs directly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Type checkboxes + date range</h3>
      <p>All nine types as checkboxes in three labeled groups, plus From / To date pickers with a presets select (03 Forms "Date range" row). Most flexible; heavier, needs date validation, bigger diff.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Three views + "week starting" date</h3>
      <p>Same radio group as A, but the week is chosen with one date picker; the table shows that day plus the next six. Any 7-day window, not just calendar weeks.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

